  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "The $n$ terms summed on the left-hand side of the equation below are in arithmetic progression:\n\n$$13+28+\\cdots+a_n=68\\,210.$$\n\nDetermine $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$n=95$.",
      "worked": "The first term is $a=13$ and the common difference is $d=15$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}S_n&=\\frac{n}{2}[2a+(n-1)d]\\\\68\\,210&=\\frac{n}{2}[26+15(n-1)]\\\\136\\,420&=n(15n+11)\\\\15n^2+11n-136\\,420&=0\\\\(n-95)(15n+1436)&=0\\\\n&=95\\quad\\text{or}\\quad n=-\\frac{1436}{15}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $n$ is a positive integer, $n=95$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
